 "lupus": "Solved in part. All 60 primary misses were the same kind: the planted source was outshone by a brighter neighbour, because the cloud's own sky is 5.5 times noisier than the pipeline variance says (1.2 times in the quiet control). Alone, the planted sources were bright enough: 20 of 20 at twice the limit. Modelling that structured sky moves Lupus III's honest 5\u03c3 limit up by a factor of 3.1; injected at that limit, 7 and 5 of 20 are found at one and two times, instead of 0. The primary rule is unchanged."
